description:
 This is a combined synopsis/solicitation for commercial products or commercial services prepared in accordance with part 12.&nbsp;This announcement constitutes the only solicitation. Offers are being requested and a separate written solicitation will not be issued. &nbsp; 

 Solicitation number N3225327Q0011 is issued as an RFQ for flow meter verification testing. 

 This acquisition is not a set-aside for small business concerns. This solicitation incorporates provisions and clauses by reference. The full text of provisions and clauses may be accessed electronically at www.acquisition.gov. 

 The Pearl Harbor Naval Shipyard and Intermediate Maintenance Facility (PHNSY &amp; IMF) is seeking a contractor to provide a manufacturer-authorized technician to conduct a noninvasive flow meter verification test for six (total) Siemens Sitrans FM MAG 5000 series meters in accordance with the attached Performance Work Statement (PWS).&nbsp; 

 The period of performance for the base year is 12/11/2026 - 12/10/2027.&nbsp; 

 The applicable North American Industry Classification Systems (NAICS) code assigned to this procurement is&nbsp;811310 Commercial and Industrial Machinery and Equipment (except Automotive and Electronic) Repair and Maintenance. Product Service Code is&nbsp;J049- Maint/Repair/Rebuild of Equipment&mdash;Maintenance and Repair Shop Equipment.&nbsp; 

 All firms or individuals responding must be registered with the System for Award Management (SAM) (https://www.sam.gov) by the award date.&nbsp; 

 Please note the following:&nbsp; 


	 The solicitation number for this requirement is N32253-27-Q-0011.&nbsp; 
	 Quotes are due not later than Friday, November 27 2026 at 0800 AM HST. 
	 Quotes must be sent via email to both primary and secondary points of contact. All firms or individuals responding must be registered with the System for Award Management (SAM) (https://sam.gov) by the award date.&nbsp; 
	 The Government may revise the solicitation at any time by means of an Amendment. It is an offeror&rsquo;s responsibility to ensure it is accessing the Government Point of Entry (GPE) website,&nbsp;https://sam.gov/, to view potential amendments and procurement notifications for this solicitation. 
	 When submitting quote, follow the solicitation instructions listed in Section L - Instructions, Conditions, &amp; Notices to Offerors or Quoters.  SEE PAGE 23 OF THE SF1449.  
	 Basis of award is listed under Section M - Evaluation Factors for Award as stated in the solicitation.  SEE PAGE 25 OF THE SF1449.  


  IMPORTANT: Please submit all quotes in accordance with the solicitation instructions.&nbsp;  

 All questions regarding this solicitation shall be submitted in writing via email to the listed POCs. Questions are due Tuesday, November 24, 2026 0800 a.m. HST.&nbsp;
